{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792846921,"nonce":"cvUVxBZqDNY9Q54gaWFJQSRae50=","title":"error_flag: a raise that stores a freshly built exception leaves the flag Unknown, so it stays in the loop","message":"In scimark SOR, every inlined G[x, y] bounds check raises IndexError on its cold arm: the exception is allocated (IndexError$new, then boxed through zb_hook_box_instance and zyntax_box_ptr) and stored into the pending-error global, and the arm branches back to the check block after the call. The error-flag dataflow counted any store of a value other than a null constant as Unknown, so those edges never reached the check as Set and were never threaded to the raising exit. The raise calls stayed inside the loop, and LICM refuses to hoist any load from a loop with an impure call, so G.width, G.data and the list headers were re-read on every access even once the alias model could tell them apart from element stores (83e67bf).\n\nThree shapes reach the store: the allocation itself, a call to the runtime's box maker, and a phi merging the box with the null that zb_hook_box_instance returns when the instance pointer is zero. The last is only dead once something knows the constructor's result is never null.\n\nFixed by counting a flag store of a value sign_fold::non_zero proves non-zero as Set, with non_zero extended to calls of functions marked returns_nonnull (inferred per body by sign_fold::record_nonnull_returns, and the runtime's box makers by link name). The same fact lets sign_fold fold the p == 0 check in the inlined box helper, and error_flag now also runs in rounds that folded something. NUC, LLVM tier, 11 interleaved reps: scimark_sor 383.5 [364.9-400.7] to 103.0 [98.7-117.5] ms, PyPy 227.3. LU, sparse matmult, FFT and the guard set within noise.","files":null}]}